.TH SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DUMMY_TIMESCALE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DUMMY_TIMESCALE \- A variable controlling the audio rate when using the dummy audio driver.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DUMMY_TIMESCALE \(dqSDL_AUDIO_DUMMY_TIMESCALE\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The dummy audio driver normally simulates real-time for the audio rate that was specified, but you can use this variable to adjust this rate higher or lower down to 0\[char46] The default value is \(dq1\[char46]0\(dq\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before an audio device is opened\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

